According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global law enforcement software market size was valued at USD 8.6 billion in 2025. Forecasts indicate the market will rise from USD 9.3 billion in 2026 to USD 16.4 billion by 2034, reflecting a CAGR of approximately 6.2 % over the forecast horizon. Growth stems from expanding adoption of digital case management tools and heightened demand for interoperable data platforms across municipal and federal agencies.
Law enforcement software encompasses integrated solutions that support police agencies in managing incident reports, criminal records, evidence tracking, and predictive analytics. Core modules such as Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD), Records Management Systems (RMS), and body camera video management enable real time information sharing across jurisdictions. Advanced analytics leverage AI based pattern recognition to assist investigators in linking crimes, while mobile applications provide officers on patrol with immediate access to critical data.
